comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-14T12:29:25.289Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 2759-item all-status CLI export with no omissions and exact PR 1257 matching found no owner. Closed pm-shpocu covers earlier action pins and is predecessor context."
  "2026-09-14T12:40:21.569Z","harness:codex","Live GitHub inventory: PR 1257 has green completed checks and four provider comments, all read and reacted to on their original surfaces. Greptile and CodeRabbit explicitly skipped the dependency author; those skips are not reviews. CodSpeed reports unchanged benchmarks and Codecov reports covered changes. The update patch is incorporated for fresh full review with this delivery. GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning open alerts are all zero; pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities. Outdated majors remain subject to established compatibility constraints."
  "2026-09-14T13:10:12.128Z","harness:codex","Tracker gate correctly rejected three new generic related edges above its ratcheted ceiling. Removed those incidental links instead of raising the bound or inventing dependency semantics. Independent major-upgrade dispositions remain documented on canonical pm-do5b, pm-fokyhh and pm-ksr40d; action-update predecessor and parent remain linked."
  "2026-09-14T13:36:12.634Z","harness:codex","Dependency eligibility verification on 2026-09-14: npm registry metadata for typescript-eslint 8.70.0 accepts TypeScript >=4.8.4 <6.1.0; CodSpeed 5.7.1 accepts Vitest ^3.2 or ^4; npm-package-arg 14 requires Node ^22.22.2 or ^24.15.0 or >=26 while pm promises >=22.18.0. The verifies edges record this concrete compatibility review of pm-do5b, pm-fokyhh and pm-ksr40d, not implementation of their upgrades."
  "2026-09-14T13:50:37.689Z","harness:codex","Final local validation: all 38 linked CI and release automation contract tests pass, full coverage and static pipeline stages pass, and pinned action updates preserve daily automatic-release idempotency. All six open GitHub issues have canonical PM links. Hosted action/security execution remains a separate required PR-head check before merge; PR 1257 will be closed as superseded after the combined delivery is available."
